[0.116694, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32mYou\u001b[0m\r\n$jevify convert workflow.py. Keep user-facing answers compact. Ask setup first.\r\n\r\n"]
[6.389333, "o", "\u001b[1;36mJevify · Codex\u001b[0m\r\nI’m using the [Jevify skill](/private/tmp/jevify-recorded-session/.agents/skills/jevify/SKILL.md). Its setup boundary requires these choices before I inspect `workflow.py`. You can use its hidden-input launcher for credentials; don’t paste secrets here.\r\n\r\n\r\n"]
[9.722527, "o", "\u001b[1;36mJevify · Codex\u001b[0m\r\nOutput location?\r\n- New branch: jev-convert/2026-09-23\r\n- Clone to a new sibling repository\r\n- Report only\r\n\r\nAccess: TypeSafe, OpenRouter, Vercel AI Gateway, or neither? Give the provider and environment-variable name only. The skill also offers a hidden-input launcher.\r\n\r\nRisk posture?\r\n- Conservative — retain original fallback everywhere\r\n- Aggressive — Jev-only where parity is proven and approved\r\n\r\n"]
[13.277828, "o", "\u001b[1;36mJevify · Codex\u001b[0m\r\nPlease answer the three setup questions above. I’ll wait before inspecting `workflow.py`.\r\n\r\n"]
[15.514732, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32mYou\u001b[0m\r\nNew branch jev-convert/demo. Neither key; conservative with the original fallback. Audit workflow.py and show the options, then wait for my approval. Keep the plan compact.\r\n\r\n"]
[21.600369, "o", "\u001b[1;36mJevify · Codex\u001b[0m\r\nI’ll check the branch setup, audit `workflow.py`, and present compact options. I’ll wait for your approval before writing files.\r\n\r\n\r\n"]
[67.039853, "o", "\u001b[1;36mJevify · Codex\u001b[0m\r\nThe repo is clean and `jev-convert/demo` is available. I found one LLM call that returns a support-ticket label. It looks suitable for a Choice trial on the bundled examples, but live parity will remain unverified without credentials.\r\n\r\n\r\n"]
[120.1712, "o", "\u001b[1;36mJevify · Codex\u001b[0m\r\nOne candidate: **ticket classification with the original fallback retained**. Preflight passed; `jev-convert/demo` is unused. No files or branches changed.\r\n\r\n| Original site | Classification / downstream use | Fit | Options |\r\n|---|---|---|---|\r\n| [workflow.py:83](/private/tmp/jevify-recorded-session/workflow.py:83) — Anthropic `claude-haiku-4-5` | **DECISION**. `simple_classify(X)` returns a stripped category string. No local callers or other LLM sites found. | Suitable for a trial on the bundled short tickets: ten fixed labels, no generated explanation. | **A — fallback:** use **Choice** for the same ten labels; retain Anthropic for low confidence, malformed responses, errors, timeouts, rate limits, or unavailable credentials. Accepted decisions should cost less and likely finish faster by avoiding generative inference; fallback calls add Jev overhead. Risk: confident misclassification; thresholds unvalidated. **B — leave:** primitive **none**; preserve this site unchanged"]
[120.171809, "o", ", with unchanged cost/latency and no migration risk. |\r\n\r\nI recommend **A**, scoped to the bundled example distribution. Public input has no effective injection mitigation; confidence alone does not resolve that limitation. See TypeSafe’s [Choice contract](https://docs.typesafe.ai/primitives/choice) and [known limitations](https://docs.typesafe.ai/model-jaggedness/jev-1.13).\r\n\r\nWith neither key selected, **live validation will be skipped** and parity cannot be claimed. The original fallback remains.\r\n\r\n**Select A or B.** I’m pausing as you requested and as [Jevify §2](/private/tmp/jevify-recorded-session/.agents/skills/jevify/SKILL.md) requires: “Do not write files until the answer.”\r\n\r\n"]
[121.767292, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32mYou\u001b[0m\r\nApprove only the pure DECISION classifier with a confidence gate and original fallback. Proceed on jev-convert/demo. No keys: explicitly skip live validation. Run the offline project smoke at /Users/bigsoup/Downloads/Jev Converter/eval/smoke.py against this repository with fixture anthropic_classification. Finish with a brief report summary. Do not push.\r\n\r\n"]
[130.572733, "o", "\u001b[1;36mJevify · Codex\u001b[0m\r\nI’ll convert only the classifier, retain the original fallback, and run the supplied offline smoke. Live validation will be explicitly skipped; I won’t push.\r\n\r\n\r\n"]
[231.664899, "o", "\u001b[1;36mJevify · Codex\u001b[0m\r\nThe classifier now has a provisional 0.95 confidence gate and the unchanged Anthropic fallback. Jev is disabled by default because no provider was selected. I’m checking fallback behavior and confirming the original request and parser are unchanged.\r\n\r\n\r\n"]
[292.411164, "o", "\u001b[1;36mJevify · Codex\u001b[0m\r\nThe supplied smoke passed. Offline checks also passed for the unchanged original request/parser, exactly-once fallback, error propagation, timeout, HTTP 429, and forced gate rejection. Live parity and accepted Jev responses remain unverified. I’m saving the report and committing locally.\r\n\r\n\r\n"]
[348.731673, "o", "\u001b[1;36mJevify · Codex\u001b[0m\r\nCommitted on `jev-convert/demo`; working tree clean. Nothing pushed.\r\n\r\n- Converted only the classifier: provisional 0.95 confidence gate, original fallback retained.\r\n- Supplied offline smoke, fault checks, and artifact checks passed.\r\n- **Live validation skipped**—no keys; parity unverified. Jev stays disabled by default.\r\n\r\n[Report](/private/tmp/jevify-recorded-session/JEV_CONVERSION_REPORT.md)\r\n\r\nUndo: `git switch main` then `git branch -D jev-convert/demo`.\r\n\r\n"]
[350.083794, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m$ git diff main -- workflow.py\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[350.10371, "o", "diff --git a/workflow.py b/workflow.py\r\nindex b839ccd..8d6b0a6 100644\r\n--- a/workflow.py\r\n+++ b/workflow.py\r\n@@ -62,7 +62,7 @@ categories = textwrap.dedent(\"\"\"<category>\r\n     </content>\r\n </category>\"\"\")\r\n \r\n-def simple_classify(X):\r\n+def _original_simple_classify(X):\r\n     prompt = (\r\n         textwrap.dedent(\"\"\"\r\n     You will classify a customer support ticket into one of the following categories:\r\n@@ -94,3 +94,9 @@ def simple_classify(X):\r\n     # Extract the result from the response\r\n     result = response.content[0].text  # pyright: ignore[reportAttributeAccessIssue]\r\n     return result.strip()\r\n+\r\n+\r\n+def simple_classify(X):\r\n+    from jev_decisions import classify\r\n+\r\n+    return classify(X, _original_simple_classify, MODEL)\r\n\r\n"]
